        "original_id": "11d3e261-8822-5bfb-ac70-0342185c40f0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kirk Humphreys, Tom Coburn, Kevin Ogle, Jim Rogers, Mike Turpen\n- Roles: Mayor of Oklahoma City, United States Senator, moderator, panelist, politician, medical doctor\n- Organizations: Democratic Party\n- Places: Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, United States\n- Programs: Flashpoint\n\nFacts:\n- Tom Coburn was born on March 14, 1948, and he is an American politician and medical doctor.\n- Kirk Humphreys was born on September 13, 1950, and he is an American politician.\n- Kirk Humphreys served as Mayor of Oklahoma City from April 9, 1998 to November 3, 2003.\n- Kevin Ogle serves as moderator of the locally produced Sunday morning political affairs talk show Flashpoint.\n- Mike Turpen and former Oklahoma City mayor Kirk Humphreys serve as panelists on Flashpoint alongside Kevin Ogle.\n- In 2010, Jim Rogers was the Democratic Party nominee for the United States Senate in Oklahoma.\n- In 2010, Jim Rogers ran against incumbent Senator Tom Coburn in the Oklahoma United States Senate race.",
